I added `writeOff(day)` to `Invoice`, just before the private `mustBeDraft` helper. It reads `owedPence()`, returns 0 without raising a note if nothing is owed, and otherwise calls `this.credit(day, owed, "written off")` and returns the amount.

I couldn't see the file body, so I anchored on the `mustBeDraft` line as I guessed it, with two-space indent. If that line differs, or a doc comment sits directly above it, the edit may be refused or the comment may end up above the new method. I also assumed `credit` doesn't change what `owedPence()` reports in a way that would make the returned amount differ from the note.
